     1|/**
     2| * IVX Amazon SES email sender (owner-only outreach delivery).
     3| *
     4| * Replaces SendGrid as the active outbound email path. Sends a single email via
     5| * the AWS SES v2 API (`/v2/email/outbound-emails`) using a SigV4-signed HTTPS
     6| * request — no new dependencies, same signing pattern as the CloudFront agent.
     7| *
     8| * Credentials come from the existing AWS env (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID /
     9| * AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / AWS_REGION). The verified sender address comes from
    10| * IVX_SES_FROM_EMAIL (falling back to OWNER_REPAIR_EMAIL / EXPO_PUBLIC_OWNER_EMAIL).
    11| *
    12| * SAFETY: callers must enforce owner approval before invoking this. This module
    13| * only performs the transport — it never decides whether a message may be sent.
    14| */
    15|import { createHash, createHmac } from 'node:crypto';
